This is the rad_astro-write-a-block package meant as a guide to building
out-of-tree packages. To use the rad_astro blocks, the Python namespaces
is in 'rad_astro', which is imported as:

    import rad_astro

See the Doxygen documentation for details about the blocks available
in this package. A quick listing of the details can be found in Python
after importing by using:

    help(rad_astro)

# Build commands
gr_modtool bind avg
to rebind python bindings.

run ldconfig to reload live into gnuradio.

# Bugs
Known issue where filewriter writes zeros for the first iteration.  Not sure why work is called with zeros in the buffers.

# rad_astro avg:
Intended to sum vectors of FFT magnitude data but can be used to sum any real vectors over multiple iterations.

Chaining these together is advised when very large integration times are needed.

# filewriter
Writes raw floating point values to a file but keeps track of UTC epoch time in milliseconds for each recording that goes into the floating point binary.

In other words you get two files, one with binary data and one with timestamps according to when a vector of binary values was written to that file.

This is so you have a steady time tracking when each measurement was taken.

